# Line-ending policy (task 24.1 / N-089).
#
# WHY: binary assets that were NOT marked binary (fonts especially) were being run
# through git's CRLF<->LF conversion, which injects/strips CR bytes and CHANGES the
# stored bytes per contributor OS — e.g. the same font measured 678,869 B (LF) vs
# 688,873 B (CRLF). Because client/dist is committed, every build artifact hash then
# shifted by machine, making D-038's byte-identity check unusable across machines.
#
# FIX (root, not leaf): normalize every TEXT file to LF in the repo AND in the working
# tree, and mark every known BINARY type explicitly so git never touches its bytes.

# Default: treat everything as text, auto-detect, store + check out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Binary assets: never apply any line-ending conversion ---
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.eot   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary

# --- Explicit text (clarity; all already covered by the default) ---
*.sh    text eol=lf
